# Native correlated-Gaussian Nyström spectrum audit v1

Prospective plan, written before numerical output inspection. The active idea remains
`nystrom-permutation-validity-v1`; this is a bounded mechanism diagnostic, not a
calibration, power, or paper-validity experiment.

## Question and frozen prediction

The released implementation floors every singular value of the landmark-center
kernel at `1e-12`. A synthetic near-singular fixture in w007 changed 7.43% of the
strict permutation-score pair orderings, but occurrence in the paper workload was
unknown. The question here is whether unchanged native correlated-Gaussian workload
geometry places any center-kernel singular values below that absolute floor.

Primary prediction: across the frozen bounded sample below, at least one native
uniform-landmark center kernel will contain a singular value below `1e-12`.

- If none do, the w007 boundary remains unobserved in this native sample; do not
  develop a corrected mapping from that synthetic result alone, and proceed to the
  predeclared RFF feature/decision-semantics audit.
- If any do, the native workload touches the released floor. Preserve spectra and
  next compare released versus mathematically explicit inverse policies on those
  exact retained cases before any null-size, power, or correction claim.

## Native protocol and bounded deviation

Use author commit `ddb9b2cacc092841518c3d4e18b745f266d8f517`, specifically
`experiments_cg.py`, `samplers.py`, `utils.py`, `kernels.py`, and `nystrom.py` as
pinned in w007 `sources/nystrom_source_manifest_v2.json`. Preserve the released
defaults `n_x=n_y=2500`, `d=3`, `rho1=.5`, rho2 in
`.51,.54,.57,.60,.63,.66,.69`, and uniform landmark counts
`14,28,42,56,70,140,350,500`. Generate and pooled-standardize data with the native
functions; select each landmark set with the native `nys_inds` call and construct
the center kernel with native `RBFkernel`.

The original script draws the external 500-per-group bandwidth pilot with
`seed=None` and generates/saves a nondeterministic test-seed list. For exact
reproducibility this diagnostic freezes eight test seeds from NumPy PCG64 root
seed `20261012` and one independent tuning seed per rho2 from root seed `20261013`.
This is a prospective sample from the same generator, not recovery of the paper's
actual seeds or its 400/1000 trial ensemble.

## Measurements and controls

For every rho2 × test seed × k row, retain the complete SciPy SVD spectrum of the
native center kernel, the independent symmetric eigenvalue spectrum, counts below
the released `1e-12` floor and NumPy's default relative pseudo-inverse tolerance,
minimum/maximum singular values, condition ratio, minimum landmark distance, and
all seed/bandwidth identities. The SVD/eigenvalue cross-check is a numerical
measurement control; it does not independently reimplement the statistical test.

The analysis unit is one generated data set and landmark setting. This finite
diagnostic reports occurrence and descriptive counts only; it does not estimate a
population frequency or treat correlated k values as independent replications.

